From 5e77c67472b03d59b298d814e347f47f072ea7a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sully <sully.niu@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:24:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] stm32mp25: add trimmed defconfig for ATK STM32MP257 board

Board bring-up configuration for the ATK STM32MP257 board: eMMC boot with
the ALIENTEK MIPI panel, no NAND/NOR/SPI-NOR.

Trimmed from a savedefconfig of the full .config:

- drop the NAND/CFI-NOR/SPI-NOR/MTD/UBI driver stack and the commands
  that depend on it (CMD_MTD, CMD_NAND, CMD_SF, CMD_UBI, CMD_UBIFS,
  CMD_MTDPARTS, DFU_MTD, DFU_NAND) - the board has none of this hardware
- keep only the MMC and NOWHERE environment backends. ENV_IS_NOWHERE is
  required: env_get_location() in board/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2.c falls back
  to ENVL_NOWHERE for every boot mode whose backend is disabled
- keep only the ALIENTEK MIPI panel, drop OTM8009A/RM68200/HX8394/LVDS
- turn off SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT (saves a 32 MiB memset at boot),
  BOOTSTAGE, ANDROID_BOOT_IMAGE, CMD_CYCLIC and the BOOTM_* variants

FIT signature verification, secure boot, autoboot encryption, TFTP/DFU/
fastboot and FWU A/B are kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
